# Wallex Grid Bot - Environment Variables

## Required Environment Variables

```env
# Node.js Environment
NODE_ENV=development

# API Server
PORT=4000

# Database
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://wallex:wallex_password@localhost:5432/wallex_grid_bot

# Redis
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379

# Security
JWT_SECRET=change-me-to-secure-random-string-at-least-32-chars
ENCRYPTION_KEY=change-me-to-secure-32-char-key-for-aes-encryption

# Wallex API Configuration
WALLEX_API_BASE_URL=https://api.wallex.ir
WALLEX_WS_URL=wss://api.wallex.ir/ws
WALLEX_API_KEY_HEADER=API-Key

# Trading Configuration
ENABLE_LIVE_TRADING=false
DEFAULT_TRADING_MODE=DRY_RUN

# Market Data
STALE_PRICE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=30
REST_POLL_INTERVAL_MS=5000

# Rate Limiting
ORDER_RATE_LIMIT_PER_10S=20

# Admin User (for initial setup)
ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@example.com
ADMIN_PASSWORD=change-me

# Optional: Private WebSocket Stream Key
# WALLEX_STREAM_KEY=your-manual-stream-key-from-wallex-login

# Optional: Minimum Notional Fallback (in USDT equivalent)
MIN_NOTIONAL_FALLBACK=1

# Optional: Sub-account Client ID (for credit account trading)
# SUB_ACCOUNT_CLIENT_ID=your-sub-account-client-id
```

## Notes

1. **Never commit real API keys or secrets to version control**
2. Copy this file to `.env` and update values for your environment
3. For production, use secure random strings for JWT_SECRET and ENCRYPTION_KEY
4. ENABLE_LIVE_TRADING must be explicitly set to `true` to enable live trading
5. Default trading mode is DRY_RUN (paper trading)
6. WALLEX_STREAM_KEY is optional - if not provided, REST polling is used for private data

## Generating Secure Keys

```bash
# Generate JWT_SECRET (at least 32 characters)
openssl rand -base64 32

# Generate ENCRYPTION_KEY (32 bytes for AES-256)
openssl rand -hex 32
```
